# 基础词 Unit21
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 基础词Unit21核心词汇

{{generate}}{{/ˈdʒenəreɪt}}{{v. 产生；引起}}{{The wind turbines generate electricity for the town.}}
{{global}}{{/ˈɡləʊbl}}{{adj. 全球的；全面的}}{{Global warming is a major environmental concern.}}
{{govern}}{{/ˈɡʌvn}}{{v. 统治；管理；支配}}{{The country is governed by a democratic system.}}
{{gradual}}{{/ˈɡrædʒuəl}}{{adj. 逐渐的；渐进的}}{{There has been a gradual improvement in his health.}}
{{grant}}{{/ɡrɑːnt}}{{v./n. 授予；拨款；助学金}}{{The government granted permission for the construction.}}
{{guarantee}}{{/ˌɡærənˈtiː}}{{v./n. 保证；担保}}{{The product comes with a two-year guarantee.}}
{{handle}}{{/ˈhændl}}{{v./n. 处理；把手}}{{She handles pressure very well.}}
{{highlight}}{{/ˈhaɪlaɪt}}{{v./n. 强调；亮点}}{{The report highlights the importance of education.}}
{{identical}}{{/aɪˈdentɪkl}}{{adj. 完全相同的}}{{The two paintings look almost identical.}}
{{identify}}{{/aɪˈdentɪfaɪ}}{{v. 识别；确认}}{{The witness identified the suspect in court.}}
{{ignore}}{{/ɪɡˈnɔːr}}{{v. 忽视；不理睬}}{{He ignored the warning signs and continued driving.}}
{{illustrate}}{{/ˈɪləstreɪt}}{{v. 说明；插图}}{{The diagram illustrates the process of photosynthesis.}}
{{impact}}{{/ˈɪmpækt}}{{n./v. 影响；冲击}}{{The new policy will have a significant impact on education.}}
{{implement}}{{/ˈɪmplɪment}}{{v./n. 实施；工具}}{{The government plans to implement the new policy next year.}}
{{implication}}{{/ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn}}{{n. 含义；暗示；影响}}{{The findings have important implications for future research.}}
{{imply}}{{/ɪmˈplaɪ}}{{v. 暗示；意味着}}{{His silence implied agreement with the proposal.}}
{{impose}}{{/ɪmˈpəʊz}}{{v. 强加；征收}}{{The government imposed a tax on luxury goods.}}
{{improve}}{{/ɪmˈpruːv}}{{v. 改善；提高}}{{She worked hard to improve her English skills.}}
{{incident}}{{/ˈɪnsɪdənt}}{{n. 事件；事故}}{{The police investigated the incident thoroughly.}}
{{incline}}{{/ɪnˈklaɪn}}{{v./n. 倾向；斜面}}{{I am inclined to agree with your suggestion.}}
{{income}}{{/ˈɪnkʌm}}{{n. 收入；所得}}{{His monthly income is enough to support his family.}}
{{incredible}}{{/ɪnˈkredəbl}}{{adj. 难以置信的；惊人的}}{{The view from the top was incredible.}}
{{index}}{{/ˈɪndeks}}{{n. 索引；指数}}{{The stock market index rose by 2% today.}}
{{indicate}}{{/ˈɪndɪkeɪt}}{{v. 表明；指示}}{{The data indicates a positive trend.}}
{{individual}}{{/ˌɪndɪˈvɪdʒuəl}}{{adj./n. 个人的；个体}}{{Each individual has the right to express their opinion.}}
{{inevitable}}{{/ɪnˈevɪtəbl}}{{adj. 不可避免的；必然的}}{{Change is inevitable in a rapidly developing world.}}
{{infer}}{{/ɪnˈfɜːr}}{{v. 推断；推论}}{{We can infer from the data that sales are improving.}}
{{inflation}}{{/ɪnˈfleɪʃn}}{{n. 通货膨胀；膨胀}}{{High inflation reduces the purchasing power of consumers.}}
{{influence}}{{/ˈɪnfluəns}}{{n./v. 影响；感化}}{{Social media has a great influence on young people.}}
{{ingredient}}{{/ɪnˈɡriːdiənt}}{{n. 成分；原料}}{{Fresh ingredients make the food taste better.}}
{{initial}}{{/ɪˈnɪʃl}}{{adj./n. 最初的；首字母}}{{The initial results of the study are promising.}}
{{initiative}}{{/ɪˈnɪʃətɪv}}{{n. 主动性；倡议}}{{She took the initiative to organize the event.}}
{{innocent}}{{/ˈɪnəsnt}}{{adj. 无辜的；天真的}}{{The jury found the defendant innocent.}}
{{innovation}}{{/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn}}{{n. 创新；革新}}{{Innovation is the key to business success.}}
{{input}}{{/ˈɪnpʊt}}{{n./v. 输入；投入}}{{We need more input from the team before making a decision.}}
{{insist}}{{/ɪnˈsɪst}}{{v. 坚持；坚决要求}}{{She insisted on paying for the dinner.}}
{{inspire}}{{/ɪnˈspaɪər}}{{v. 激励；启发}}{{Her speech inspired many young people to pursue their dreams.}}
{{install}}{{/ɪnˈstɔːl}}{{v. 安装；设置}}{{They installed a new air conditioning system.}}
{{instance}}{{/ˈɪnstəns}}{{n. 例子；实例}}{{For instance, you could try a different approach.}}
{{instinct}}{{/ˈɪnstɪŋkt}}{{n. 本能；直觉}}{{Animals rely on instinct to find food.}}
{{institute}}{{/ˈɪnstɪtjuːt}}{{n./v. 学院；制定}}{{The research institute published a groundbreaking study.}}
{{institution}}{{/ˌɪnstɪˈtjuːʃn}}{{n. 机构；制度}}{{Universities are important educational institutions.}}
{{instrument}}{{/ˈɪnstrəmənt}}{{n. 仪器；乐器}}{{She plays several musical instruments.}}
{{intellectual}}{{/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl}}{{adj./n. 智力的；知识分子}}{{Intellectual property is protected by law.}}
{{intelligence}}{{/ɪnˈtelɪdʒəns}}{{n. 智力；情报}}{{Artificial intelligence is advancing rapidly.}}
{{intend}}{{/ɪnˈtend}}{{v. 打算；想要}}{{We intend to finish the project by December.}}
{{intense}}{{/ɪnˈtens}}{{adj. 强烈的；紧张的}}{{The competition was intense.}}
{{intention}}{{/ɪnˈtenʃn}}{{n. 意图；目的}}{{He had no intention of leaving the company.}}
{{interact}}{{/ˌɪntərˈækt}}{{v. 互动；相互作用}}{{Children learn by interacting with their peers.}}
{{interfere}}{{/ˌɪntəˈfɪər}}{{v. 干涉；妨碍}}{{Please do not interfere with my work.}}
{{internal}}{{/ɪnˈtɜːnl}}{{adj. 内部的；国内的}}{{The company resolved its internal conflicts.}}
{{interpret}}{{/ɪnˈtɜːprɪt}}{{v. 解释；口译}}{{Different people may interpret the poem differently.}}
{{interrupt}}{{/ˌɪntəˈrʌpt}}{{v. 打断；中断}}{{It is rude to interrupt someone while they are speaking.}}
{{introduce}}{{/ˌɪntrəˈdjuːs}}{{v. 介绍；引进}}{{The company introduced a new product to the market.}}
{{investigate}}{{/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt}}{{v. 调查；研究}}{{The police are investigating the cause of the fire.}}
{{invest}}{{/ɪnˈvest}}{{v. 投资；投入}}{{She invested a large sum in the stock market.}}
{{involve}}{{/ɪnˈvɒlv}}{{v. 涉及；包含；使参与}}{{The project involves a lot of teamwork.}}
{{isolate}}{{/ˈaɪsəleɪt}}{{v. 隔离；孤立}}{{The patient was isolated to prevent the spread of disease.}}
{{issue}}{{/ˈɪʃuː}}{{n./v. 问题；发行；发布}}{{Climate change is a global issue.}}
{{justify}}{{/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ}}{{v. 证明…正当；为…辩护}}{{How can you justify spending so much money?}}
